                                "sense_id": "22ebdfdb-c990-3d0d-81c0-17a52cc423ba",
                                "text": "There are several recursion theorems for large sets, such that a single new halving results in several new infinite families of halvings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3112c40-5782-48c0-90b6-fc2185e6539d",
                                "sense_id": "22ebdfdb-c990-3d0d-81c0-17a52cc423ba",
                                "text": "Similitude applies to proportional changes, such as doublings, halvings, or quarterings; it does not apply to additive changes."
                            }
                        ]
